  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of people reached by newly trained health care workers through health facilities and community outreach</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zero (0)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conduct of post intervention assessment to understand the impact of project intervention
Provision of medical equipment, related logistics and completion of CHPS Compound in Chorkor
Improved home visits for newly trained Community health officers in Ga Central and Accra Metropolitan Area</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post intervention assessment conducted to understand the impact of project interventions revealed an improvement in the knowledge of health care workers and increased uptake of health services for the vulnerable especially for NCDs and HIV in selected districts as a result of project interventions. Provision of medical equipment and logistics to CHPS and health facilities in Ga Central and Accra metro has enhanced service delivery for the vulnerable. In addition, the provision of CHPS compound in Chorkor and a modular patient block in Anyaa polyclinic has brought essential health services closer to the vulnerable communities. Furthermore, community health officers who received training as part of the project conducted over 9,000 home visits in Accra Metro and Ga Central districts to provide much needed health service to the vulnerable.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A thousand (1,000)
(600F/400M)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through UNDP support, 100 (67 women, 33 Men) community health management committee members, community health volunteers and community health officers in Ga central and Accra Metro have improved knowledge and skills to strengthen equitable and essential health service provision for the vulnerable within their communities</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
